From 52df6af62cc3509b1db41c46611c035c60eae46e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 21:23:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] msm_mtp: Support configfs/UDC gadgets and start umtprd

Modern kernels (Halium 9 and later, and every mainline kernel) configure
the USB gadget through configfs/libcomposite; /sys/class/android_usb and
the f_mtp misc device do not exist there, so the module never reported
the MTP "driver" as available and Mass Storage Mode was dead on such
devices.

Keep the android_usb path for legacy kernels and add a configfs path:

- driver available: a UDC exists in /sys/class/udc and umtprd is
  installed (its ffs.mtp function is created on demand at start)
- host connected: any UDC reports state configured (or suspended)
- change notifications: also subscribe to "udc" uevents, which carry
  USB_STATE on gadget state transitions

The MTP daemon started on enable is now umtprd (uMTP-Responder), which
speaks FunctionFS directly and replaces the libhybris-based mtp-server.
State reads use plain sysfs instead of libudev object lookups, and the
udev event handler now unrefs the received device (it leaked before) and
checks that a change callback was registered before invoking it.
---
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS specific]

 src/msm_mtp/msm.c | 178 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 1 file changed, 121 insertions(+), 57 deletions(-)

